// mdnsresolve.mtl — resolve ".local" names over multicast mDNS instead of
// unicast DNS to the gateway.
//
// Why: some gateways silently drop a single client's unicast DNS queries (a
// per-client ACL / DNS-flood guard). The rabbit then loops forever on
// `A? <xmpp-domain>` and never reaches XMPP — it stays all-orange. mDNS
// sidesteps the gateway entirely: a ".local" query goes to the multicast group
// 224.0.0.251:5353 and any responder on the segment (e.g. avahi on the HA host)
// answers it. No gateway DNS, no reply-spoofing.
//
// How it plugs in: dns.mtl's `dnsreq` already builds a perfectly ordinary DNS A
// query and (unpatched) sends it to `netdns:53`. We change ONLY the destination
// when the name ends in ".local": send it to the mDNS group instead. Because our
// source port stays DNSLOCAL (1597, != 5353), an RFC 6762 §6.7 responder treats
// it as a "legacy unicast query" and unicasts the answer back to :1597 with our
// query id echoed — so dns.mtl's existing `cbnetdns` matches and parses it with
// zero changes. The canonical multicast MAC (01:00:5e:00:00:fb, RFC 1112 §6.4)
// lets `udpsend` skip arpreq for the class-D address.
//
// Pairs with the add-on: locate.jsp must return a ".local" xmpp domain and a
// responder on the HA host must answer it. The announcer (mdns.mtl) is the
// opposite direction (publishes the rabbit) and is unrelated to this.
//
// VLAN caveat: mDNS doesn't cross VLANs by default. If HA sits on another VLAN
// than the rabbit, enable an mDNS reflector for that group on the switch/router
// (UniFi: per-network "Multicast DNS").
//
// Constants are namespaced (MDNSR_*) so they never clash with mdns.mtl's
// announcer constants, whatever the include order is.

// 224.0.0.251
const MDNSR_IP="\224\0\0\$fb";;
const MDNSR_PORT=5353;;
// 01:00:5e:00:00:fb — the multicast MAC for 224.0.0.251.
const MDNSR_MAC="\1\0\$5e\0\0\$fb";;

// True if `s` ends in ".local" (case-sensitive — locate controls the name).
// strcmp returns 0 when equal, so `!strcmp a b` reads "a equals b".
fun mdnsr_islocal s=
	let strlen s -> n in
	if n<6 then 0
	else !strcmp (strsub s n-6 nil) ".local";;
